      "message": "Note for Greg (leaving as unresolved for visibility):\n\nIn case you\u0027re wondering, I skip checking for MSAA here because we now perform this check when determining which `DstReadStrategy` should be used by both the `DrawPass` and the `RenderPassDesc`. Relevant comment and bug ID mentioned there now instead (and will be removed once MSAA dst texture reads are supported): https://skia.googlesource.com/skia.git/+/refs/heads/main/src/gpu/graphite/DrawContext.cpp#212\n\nFor more context if you\u0027re interested:\nBefore elevating that decision to the `DrawContext` level, a `DrawPass` could have a target texture that is single-sampled (which means Vulkan would report we are able to use `kReadFromInput`). However, when creating the `RenderPassDesc`, we check for `msaaRenderToSingleSampledSupport` and then may decide to make the target multisampled. This elevation aligned the two and allowed us to remove `TextureInfo` as a parameter to `getDstReadStrategy` already (which was planned to happen eventually anyhow), which was helpful for precompilation(+).\n\n(+) without making this comment into a research paper, this is basically because it enables us to remove `DstReadStrategy` from `RenderPassDesc` serialization since we can re-determine what strategy to use upon deserialization even though we do not have the target texture information at that time. This way, precompilation `RenderPassDesc`s appropriately ignore `DstReadStrategy` for unique keying. This behavior is desired because the resulting pipeline compilation is the same either way (for Vulkan as well since DstReadStrategy::kNone and kReadFromInput have shared compatible RPs).",
